{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521015-a-first-edition-chronicle-ideas-needed","id":1521015,"title":"A first edition chronicle, ideas needed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-20T01:47:52-07:00","id":1521015,"title":"A first edition chronicle, ideas needed","content":"I bought the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/149035/Mage-The-Ascension-First-Edition?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">first edition of Mage the Ascension</a> in the Summer of Darkness sale, and it looks quite interesting. If I remember correctly, there was quite an edition war with the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/200/Mage-The-Ascension-Second-Edition?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">second edition</a>, with changes in setting and in how magic(k) worked. The two later editions seem to have taken further steps from the first edition's ideas and assumptions. It is partially described in the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/248790/Mage-The-Ascension-Storytellers-Vault-Style-Guide?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">style guide</a>.<br /> <br /> Now, I am thinking of creating a first edition chronicle for my players. They do know Mage the Ascension, but later editions. Is it going to be quite a big shift in experiencing Mage, in your opinion? What are the strengths of the first edition? Is there some experience or idea in the game you think I should avoid? Some to embrace? Which books are particularly apt to use for a first edition chronicle? Did Mage the Ascension's first edition chronicle in San Francisco receive any support besides the brief story in the main book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T23:20:56-07:00","id":1521100,"title":"","content":"I imagine that Study points could be an issue worth considering. The idea was removed in later editions, but in the first edition it gave the feeling of mages devoting time for developing themselves.<br /> <br /> Then again, Study points might be a too dry concept to describe this development in the stories? Did you use Study points, and what do you think would be the best way to replace them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T14:55:27-07:00","id":1521285,"title":"","content":"I assume you're talking about the All Hallow's Eve adventure in the back of the Rulebook. As it said at the start of it, it's the start of the larger Loom of Fate adventure. It's a decent enough adventure though like much of early 1E, suffers from the devs not quite knowing here they want to go with MtAs* and some things being a weird and gonzo compared to what even 2E and late 1E would have. You can pick it up individually or in a combined book with the Chaos Factor cross-splat adventure.<br /> <br /> *Which from what I've heard, it was a general problem that all WoD suffered from but MtAs in particular suffered from. Like the 1E Rulebook was a rush job after the initial draft ended up being a real mess and had to be redone. And having read some of the 1E books, I can see that MtAs could be kind of all over the place in it's early days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T05:59:35-07:00","id":1521324,"title":"","content":"Weird and gonzo is the flavor of the day! Thank you! Now I understand the relationship between the two stories better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T06:50:31-07:00","id":1521505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cabaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521015-a-first-edition-chronicle-ideas-needed#post1521015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bought the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/149035/Mage-The-Ascension-First-Edition?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">first edition of Mage the Ascension</a> in the Summer of Darkness sale, and it looks quite interesting. If I remember correctly, there was quite an edition war with the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/200/Mage-The-Ascension-Second-Edition?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">second edition</a>, with changes in setting and in how magic(k) worked. The two later editions seem to have taken further steps from the first edition's ideas and assumptions. It is partially described in the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/248790/Mage-The-Ascension-Storytellers-Vault-Style-Guide?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">style guide</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, every new edition of Mage sparked some issues.<br /> <br /> The 2nd edition basically rebooted the setting, which, while I prefer the way it is since that edition, is to me the root of most problems of lore consistency in Mage.<br /> Revised edition gutted a massive chunk of the game, forcing street level survival as a basis, and made magic, the very core of a game called &quot;Mage&quot;, better to avoid using.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAs for M20, well, it was a kickstarter disaster, and is polluted by an author taking too much freedom with what he has to write down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T20:03:56-07:00","id":1521570,"title":"","content":"When I think of first edition Mage, I think of <i>Ars Magica</i>. <br /> <br /> Later edition took away Study-points? Well, I'll have to put them back. <br /> <br /> So, with Mage, you're dealing with a lot of characters that can fabricate their own reality, so, a mage-game is like playing in an insane-asylum.<br /> <br /> Most of the mage-games I ran took place in the past (Dark Ages/Antiquity), so, it was basically <i>Ars Magica</i>, with Mage-rules (Storyteller). Being that, I had a player that wanted to be a, &quot;Fighter&quot;, so, he made a standard mage-character, sans magic. <br /> <br /> As for which book, just the basic rule-book will do for starters; if you like a particular-faction, then get that book. I, for one. like the Order of Hermes, so, I got that book. Back in the day, I would go to the local used-bookstore and find random RPG books to use. I got the player's guide to mage; it didn't change my life, sadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T08:13:02-07:00","id":1521592,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Book of Shadows&quot; it's MtA 1e players book. I think it's actually a very good and interesting read for players and ST alike.<br /> <br /> It IS going to be a big shift.<br /> <br /> A lot of the rules - and even assumptions - they may be accustomed to, will not be the same. A lot of rules you may expect to find just won't be there. For instance:<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly: there's not a rule about &quot;rituals&quot; on the core. Because there wasn't rituals, the &quot;table of successes&quot; works very different. There's not a general table that goes from 1 to 20+ (that would be quite impossible w/o rituals). Rather there's one table per Sphere, that also doubles as general effect-per-success rules, determining what you should be able to accomplish.<br /> <br /> I remember to play 1e once, and had the assuption was that you could get out with whatever the sphere said at al level with a number of successes equal to that level (like 3 successes for anything that Sphere 3 can do). Probably that was just our house rule. Yet, because the &quot;tables of successes&quot; don't cover everything that you may want to do with a Sphere, i think you may end wanting to rule something similar for the &quot;uncovered&quot; cases<br /> <br /> So, if I were to attempt that, I would embrace to expect the unexpected, and think may end having to make rulings on the fly (well, more so than it's usual on Mage)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-29-2023, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T18:59:25-07:00","id":1521713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521015-a-first-edition-chronicle-ideas-needed?p=1521592#post1521592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Book of Shadows&quot; it's MtA 1e players book. I think it's actually a very good and interesting read for players and ST alike.<br /> <br /> . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what it's called!!! I guess I was too lazy to walk across my room and look on my bookshelf (my room is big). <br /> <br /> Book of Shadows really didn't inspire me, unlike the Ascension core-book. I find myself going back and rereading that book often (to the point, my first one fell apart and I got another one). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}